      en: ["Inscribed as a UNESCO World Heritage site in 1998.", "Served as the Maronite Patriarchate's seat from 1440 to 1823.", "Home to the Deir Qannoubine monastery, established in the 4th century.", "The name originates from the Greek word 'Coenobium,' meaning monastery.", "One of the most significant Christian mountain refuges in the Middle East.", "Famous for its rock-cut churches featuring medieval religious frescoes."],
