      en: ["Byblos has been continuously inhabited since the 5th millennium BC.", "The city was inscribed as a UNESCO World Heritage site in 1984.", "The Crusader Castle was constructed in 1104 by the Franks.", "The name 'Byblos' is the Greek word for 'book' or 'papyrus'.", "Contains the Temple of the Obelisks, dating to the 19th century BC.", "The ancient harbor was the primary terminal for Phoenician cedar trade."],
