      en: ["Home to 22 inscriptions and stelae spanning several millennia.", "The oldest stela was carved by Pharaoh Ramses II in the 13th century BC.", "Added to the UNESCO Memory of the World Register in 2005.", "The name 'Nahr al-Kalb' translates to 'Dog River' in Arabic.", "Esarhaddon of Assyria left inscriptions here in the 7th century BC.", "The valley features a historic Ottoman-era stone bridge."],
